    <summary>In 2022, Gezmis and Pellarin introduced and studied the concept of trivial multiple zeta values, along with a map from the vector space spanned by these values to the vector space spanned by Thakur's multiple zeta values. Their construction allows us to generate some linear relations among the latter values using the former. In our work, we determine the structure of the kernel of the aforementioned map. As a consequence, we give an answer to a conjecture proposed by Gezmis and Pellarin regarding the injectivity of this specific map.</summary>
