  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2308.16808v4</id>
    <title>Towards the Overfull Conjecture</title>
    <updated>2024-09-05T21:14:20Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.16808v4" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2308.16808v4" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Let $G$ be a simple graph with maximum degree denoted as $Δ(G)$. An overfull subgraph $H$ of $G$ is a subgraph satisfying the condition $|E(H)| &gt; Δ(G)\lfloor \frac{1}{2}|V(H)| \rfloor$. In 1986, Chetwynd and Hilton proposed the Overfull Conjecture, stating that a graph $G$ with maximum degree $Δ(G)&gt; \frac{1}{3}|V(G)|$ has chromatic index equal to $Δ(G)$ if and only if it does not contain any overfull subgraph. The Overfull Conjecture has many implications. For example, it implies a polynomial-time algorithm for determining the chromatic index of graphs $G$ with $Δ(G) &gt; \frac{1}{3}|V(G)|$, and implies several longstanding conjectures in the area of graph edge colorings. In this paper, we make the first breakthrough towards the conjecture when not imposing a minimum degree condition on the graph: for any $0&lt;\varepsilon \le \frac{1}{14}$, there exists a positive integer $n_0$ such that if $G$ is a graph on $n\ge n_0$ vertices with $Δ(G) \ge (1-\varepsilon)n$, then the Overfull Conjecture holds for $G$. The previous best result in this direction, due to Chetwynd and Hilton from 1989, asserts the conjecture for graphs $G$ with $Δ(G) \ge |V(G)|-3$. Our result also implies the Average Degree Conjecture of Vizing from 1968 for the same class of graphs $G$.</summary>
    <category term="math.CO" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2023-08-31T15:33:13Z</published>
